{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5iGNnGFTwwTj4iXAB8o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my exploration, I have a comprehensive understanding of the repository structure and conventions. Let me now state my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt`\n- ShipmentStatus enum: line 23-27 (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: line 20-56 showing create/get/list patterns\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt` with save/findById/existsById/findAll methods\n- Error handling: ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) in `ApiExceptions.kt`\n- Error codes enum: `ApiError.kt` line 31-37 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: centralized exception-to-response conversion\n- Tests: `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` using MockMvc and jsonPath assertions\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses instead of returning error responses directly\n- Error responses use a standardized envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": []}}`\n- `POST` endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...)`\n- Tests use `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, MockMvc with MockMvcRequestBuilders\n- Repository operations: `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()`, `findAll()`, `clear()`\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - Need to add a new error code for invalid shipment state (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - Need to add the confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Need to add tests for the confirm functionality\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency must be handled correctly (confirming already-confirmed shipment must succeed)\n- The CANCELLED → CONFIRMED transition must be rejected with 409 CONFLICT\n- Must preserve existing test passing status\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - the requirement is clear about all cases.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** (line 31-37): Add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in CANCELLED status.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** (line 20-56): Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Takes a `shipmentId` path variable\n   - Retrieves the shipment from repository\n   - If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException` with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE`\n   - If status is CREATED, save it with CONFIRMED status\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, no-op (just return it)\n   - Returns the shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** (line 23-84): Add four new test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment → transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment → succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment → returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment → returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered not adding a new error code and reusing `VALIDATION_FAILED` for the CANCELLED case. Rejected because: (1) VALIDATION_FAILED is for input validation, not state conflicts; (2) SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE is more semantically precise for a conflict with the resource's current state; (3) adding an enum value is minimal and aligns with the pattern of having specific error codes for specific failure modes.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Case: Confirm CREATED shipment**\n  - Read: existing shipment from repository\n  - Write: save shipment with CONFIRMED status\n  - Return: 200 OK with updated shipment\n\n- **Case: Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment**\n  - Read: existing shipment from repository\n  - Write: save shipment with CONFIRMED status (no-op)\n  - Return: 200 OK with shipment\n\n- **Case: Confirm CANCELLED shipment**\n  - Read: existing shipment from repository\n  - Write: none\n  - Exception: ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) → GlobalExceptionHandler → 409 with error body\n\n- **Case: Confirm non-existent shipment**\n  - Read: repository returns null\n  - Exception: ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) → GlobalExceptionHandler → 404 with error body\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Happy path - confirm a CREATED shipment and verify status changes to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Idempotent - confirm twice and verify second call succeeds\n- Test 3: Invalid state - set up CANCELLED shipment via direct repository write, attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n- Test 4: Not found - attempt confirm on non-existent ID, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nI'll now implement the changes. First, add the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":16224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":829},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9444598-dff2-4788-868c-4148932d2274","uuid":"afca8aac-a036-4ea3-b00a-f3635a1a1763","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:39:13.178Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5iGNFWfpvbUXivu9aBM"}
